<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Port Louis</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Port Louis is the capital and main harbour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mauritius">Mauritius</a>. It was developed from 1735 by the French governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahe-de-la-bourdonnais">Mahé de La Bourdonnais</a> as the capital and naval base of Isle de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. After the British conquest of 1810 it remained the seat of government of British Mauritius and the centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> trade.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/port-louis.jpg" alt="Port Louis" width="320" height="187" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thierry · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Port_Louis_Skyline.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
